+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Common base following time for the selected GAP level. The planner’s applied time, including speed, driving-mode and braking adjustments, also drives Porter button deceleration and optional low-target cancellation.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Porter dedicated GAP OFF uses these common values. ON selects Porter GAP1–4 for both planner and button decisions without copying or resetting either set of saved values.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Without a fresh valid planner time, use the selected mode’s base setting. The existing 7m distance floor and button/cancel bounds remain; actual following distance, braking or stopping is not guaranteed.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
